Camera to the EP (2026-10-12): the one-view reference camera starts at the fighters' middle, not at START_X + 350.
Two files that are not Camera's (Simulation's sim/core/view/camera.gd under the sim's gate; render/core/sim_host.gd is Rendering's).
The class-level defaults stay (the goldens construct SimCamera.new() with no reset, so they are unchanged); only reset() gains an
optional state, and the host passes it. A match that starts at a downtown crossing (WorldLanes.demoStartX) puts the camera on the
pair on its first frame instead of panning 40,000 units from the desert's west edge.

--- a/sim/core/view/camera.gd
+++ b/sim/core/view/camera.gd
@@ -15,9 +15,18 @@
 var z: float = 0.45
 
 
-func reset() -> void:
-	x = SimConst.START_X + 350.0
-	y = 100.0
-	z = 0.45
+## `S` is the match's state when the host has one: the camera starts on the fighters' middle (a match that starts at a
+## downtown crossing, or anywhere but the desert's edge, is framed from its first frame). Without it, the old default.
+func reset(S: SimState = null) -> void:
+	x = SimConst.START_X + 350.0
+	y = 100.0
+	z = 0.45
+	if S != null and S.fighters.size() >= 2:
+		var a = S.fighters[0]
+		var b = S.fighters[1]
+		x = SimWrap.wrap(a.x + SimWrap.sdx(a.x, b.x) / 2.0)
+		y = SimMathx.jclamp((a.y + b.y) / 2.0 + 40.0, -180.0, SimConst.CEILING - 200.0)
 
--- a/render/core/sim_host.gd
+++ b/render/core/sim_host.gd
@@ -81,1 +81,1 @@
-	cam.reset()
+	cam.reset(S)
